<h1>Jobs Administration</h1>

<p>This page allows administrators to manage job execution across the entire StarExec system.
From here, you can pause or resume all job processing system-wide.</p>

<h2>Pause All Jobs</h2>

<p>The "pause all" button will pause all job execution across the entire StarExec system.
This means that no new job pairs will be dequeued or executed on the compute nodes.
Currently running job pairs will continue to completion, but no new pairs will start.</p>

<p>This feature is useful for:</p>
<ul>
<li>System maintenance - preventing new jobs from starting while performing maintenance</li>
<li>Emergency situations - stopping job execution if issues are detected with the cluster</li>
<li>Resource management - temporarily halting job processing to free up resources</li>
</ul>

<h2>Resume All Jobs</h2>

<p>The "resume all" button will resume normal job execution across the StarExec system.
Job pairs that were queued while the system was paused will begin processing normally.</p>

<p>Note: Individual jobs can still be paused or resumed independently using their respective
job detail pages, even when the system-wide pause is not active.</p>

<h2>Jobs Table</h2>

<p>The jobs table displays all jobs in the system with administrative information including
job status, owner, execution statistics, and other relevant details for system monitoring.</p>
